{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"bin/render must run with an otherwise empty environment containing only PATH=/usr/bin:/bin, from any working directory, locate the supplied helper and template, and write the requested output with the complete report contents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired launcher resolves the application directory from its own location and invokes the supplied helper and template by absolute paths. Direct tests from unrelated directories (/tmp and /) under env -i with only the required PATH succeeded, created the requested relative or absolute output, and exactly matched the expected report. The same behavior was confirmed after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eec2b3c81bac4c0e","cmd-e1498dd0dc2e4056","cmd-2fa347c23f0241c2","cmd-1437296706d44e95"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve the source template under /srv/legacy2/minimal-environment-job.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The template retained its baseline SHA-256 hash and original Region/Shipments content after the repair and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-3022db05f7bc4db4","cmd-e1498dd0dc2e4056","cmd-1437296706d44e95"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CentOS Stream 10 and kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 remained unchanged. The implementation uses the existing POSIX shell and standard utilities, with no package installation or platform replacement observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-813088ee2e044499","cmd-eec2b3c81bac4c0e","cmd-1437296706d44e95","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles: editing bin/render implemented the repair; generating reports collected bounded functional/restart evidence; and rebooting fulfilled the provider-wide restart protocol. No unrelated or reverted troubleshooting mutations were identified. The restart protocol is strong: the pre-restart boot ID and working render were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, the system recovered to running state, and the application, template, OS, and kernel were revalidated; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree. Hygiene is reduced because evidence artifacts were left behind: /tmp/render-verify.31Wevi with requested-report.txt and /tmp/render-restart-baseline.out remained, and /var/tmp/render-after-reboot.out was created without demonstrated cleanup. System services, sockets, and package health otherwise remained healthy; socket differences are only post-reboot process descriptors.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eec2b3c81bac4c0e","cmd-e1498dd0dc2e4056","cmd-2fa347c23f0241c2","cmd-7ad150349440483c","cmd-2492130085b14d6a","cmd-1437296706d44e95","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence, including persistence across the mandatory node restart. The only notable deficiency is minor retained verification-output residue.","limitations":["Lifecycle file inventory is bounded to /tmp, so it does not independently confirm cleanup or retention of the directly observed /var/tmp/render-after-reboot.out.","The evidence demonstrates operation from multiple unrelated working directories rather than literally every possible directory, which is a reasonable behavioral test of the self-locating implementation."]}
